<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  DDS configuration for the car.

  NOT the answer to the 0.3 s stalls. Those were measured on a run of
  head_to_head, where htop showed all six cores at 100% and a load average
  of 10.97 - the gaussian process predictor alone was taking about two and
  a half of them while the particle filter got 38%. A machine oversubscribed
  by 180% stalls, and no dds setting changes that. Read that history in the
  commit that added this file; the reasoning there was wrong.

  What is left, and why this is still worth having: FastDDS is Humble's
  default and UNIST measured it busy-spinning a whole core against
  CycloneDDS idling at ~21% on their node set. time_trials brings up 21
  nodes. That is real overhead on a jetson whose particle filter is already
  scan-limited, it is simply not what was making the car stall.

  The interface list is the other half. /scan is published RELIABLE -
  deliberately, because a best-effort publisher starves a reliable
  subscriber silently - and reliable means the publisher retransmits until
  the subscriber acknowledges, so a laptop watching over wifi couples its
  own packet loss back into the car. Naming the interfaces keeps discovery
  off the link that has nothing on it.

  Interfaces are therefore listed explicitly rather than autodetected:

    127.0.0.1   the whole stack is one host; this is the path that matters
    wlan0       the laptop. RENAME IT if `ip -br link` says otherwise.

  enP8p1s0 is deliberately absent. That is the lidar's private 192.168.0.x
  link with nothing on it but the sensor, and discovery traffic there is
  pure waste.

  Used as:
    export RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_cyclonedds_cpp
    export CYCLONEDDS_URI="file://$HOME/roboracer_unita_ws/cyclonedds.xml"

  If the freezes persist with the laptop connected, the next step is to stop
  sending /scan over the air at all - view it through the foxglove bridge,
  which is one TCP connection that cannot push back into the publisher's DDS
  the way a reliable DDS subscriber does.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
    <Domain id="any">
        <General>
            <Interfaces>
                <NetworkInterface address="127.0.0.1" multicast="true"/>
                <NetworkInterface name="wlan0" multicast="true" presence_required="false"/>
            </Interfaces>
            <AllowMulticast>true</AllowMulticast>
        </General>
        <Discovery>
            <ParticipantIndex>none</ParticipantIndex>
        </Discovery>
        <Internal>
            <SocketReceiveBufferSize min="default"/>
            <SocketSendBufferSize min="default"/>
        </Internal>
    </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
